      "role": "tool",
      "content": "     1|# Mini-Agent Memory System\n     2|\n     3|## Persistent Memory for AI Assistants\n     4|\n     5|Transform any Mini-Agent into a persistent memory system with:\n     6|- 🧠 **Permanent session memory** across interactions\n     7|- 💾 **Multi-database storage** for redundancy\n     8|- 📊 **Intelligent analytics** and pattern detection\n     9|- 🔄 **Session continuity** across resets\n    10|- 📈 **Knowledge compounding** over time\n    11|\n    12|## Quick Start\n    13|\n    14|### Installation\n    15|```bash\n    16|# Download and extract package\n    17|# Run installer\n    18|python3 mini_agent_memory_installer.py\n    19|\n    20|# Or use setup script\n    21|cd mini-agent-memory-1.0\n    22|./setup.sh\n    23|```\n    24|\n    25|### Usage\n    26|```python\n    27|from mini_agent_memory import MiniAgentCore\n    28|\n    29|# Initialize memory\n    30|memory = MiniAgentCore(\n    31|    redis_host='localhost',\n    32|    redis_port=18000,\n    33|    password='your_password'\n    34|)\n    35|\n    36|# Start session\n    37|session = memory.start_work_session('UserName', 'ProjectContext')\n    38|\n    39|# Process interaction\n    40|result = memory.process_user_interaction(\n    41|    user_input=\"User question\",\n    42|    agent_response=\"AI response\"\n    43|)\n    44|\n    45|# Get intelligent response\n    46|response = memory.get_intelligent_response(\"Database patterns\")\n    47|```\n    48|\n    49|### Command Line\n    50|```bash\n    51|# Start memory session\n    52|mini_agent_memory start\n    53|\n    54|# Process with memory\n    55|mini_agent_memory process --user-input \"How do I build APIs?\"\n    56|\n    57|# Get analytics\n    58|mini_agent_memory analytics\n    59|```\n    60|\n    61|## Features\n    62|\n    63|### Persistent Memory\n    64|- Session continuity across resets/restarts\n    65|- Knowledge extraction from every interaction\n    66|- User preference learning\n    67|- Work progress tracking\n    68|\n    69|### Multi-Database Support\n    70|- **DragonflyDB**: High-performance primary memory\n    71|- **Redis**: Session data and chat history\n    72|- **PostgreSQL**: Structured analytics\n    73|- **ClickHouse**: Pattern analysis\n    74|- **MongoDB**: Document storage (optional)\n    75|\n    76|### Enterprise Grade\n    77|- 4x redundant storage\n    78|- Sub-10ms response times\n    79|- Real-time analytics\n    80|- Cross-database search\n    81|- Zero data loss architecture\n    82|\n    83|## Documentation\n    84|\n    85|- `INTEGRATION_GUIDE.md` - Complete integration instructions\n    86|- `API_REFERENCE.md` - Full API documentation\n    87|- `EXAMPLES/` - Integration examples\n    88|- `CONFIGS/` - Configuration templates\n    89|\n    90|## System Requirements\n    91|\n    92|### Minimum\n    93|- Python 3.7+\n    94|- Redis (for basic memory)\n    95|\n    96|### Recommended\n    97|- DragonflyDB or Redis (primary memory)\n    98|- PostgreSQL (analytics)\n    99|- ClickHouse (pattern detection)\n   100|\n   101|## License\n   102|\n   103|MIT License - Free for Mini-Agent distribution\n   104|\n   105|## Support\n   106|\n   107|- Integration issues: See INTEGRATION_GUIDE.md\n   108|- Performance: Check system health with `mini_agent_memory health`\n   109|- Database setup: Use provided Docker configurations\n   110|\n   111|---\n   112|\n   113|**Mini-Agent Memory System v1.0**  \n   114|*Built by Chase for permanent AI memory*\n   115|\n   116|🚀 **Transform your AI assistant into a persistent memory companion!**",
